  "summary": "Fixes bitcoin-wallet create to exit with an error status when wallet creation fails. Previously, ExecuteWalletToolFunc returned true after MakeWallet failed, causing the utility to exit with status 0 even on errors like an already-existing wallet database.",
  "problem": "bitcoin-wallet create reports success via its exit code (0) even when it fails to create a wallet. Scripts and automated tooling relying on the process exit code cannot detect failures such as database path collisions or creation errors.",
  "evidence": [
    "The PR description demonstrates that running `bitcoin-wallet create` twice prints 'Database already exists.' but produces exit code 0 (`echo $?` -> 0).",
    "Commit f64d33672f notes that every other subcommand in bitcoin-wallet (`info`, `dump`, `createfromdump`) returns false on failure while `create` was returning true on failure."
